bambiui repository license scope

The MIT License in packages/cli/LICENSE applies to:

1. Files in packages/cli/, including its compiled dist/ runtime and package
   documentation.
2. Exactly the shared source files enumerated in distribution-license.json.
   This is an explicit file allowlist, not a license for their parent folders.
3. Copies of those sources and bambiui-provided integration templates delivered
   through the CLI, static registry, or manual source package, accompanied by
   that MIT License and the distribution NOTICE.md.

No license to other repository files is granted by this notice. In particular,
Studio application/editor/canvas/inspector code outside the explicit allowlist
is not made open source by the CLI's MIT license. The private Next application
package is not the npm CLI package.

User-authored designs, token values, project data and content are not relicensed
by bambiui's software license. Third-party software, fonts and assets remain
subject to their own licenses. The MIT software license does not grant trademark
rights in the bambiui name or logos.

The full standard MIT terms and copyright notice are in packages/cli/LICENSE.
See docs/licensing.md for distribution boundaries and maintenance instructions.
